h3 2.3.2 Boolean attributes @17,1497,694,19
text A number of attributes are . The presence of a boolean attribute on an element represents the true value, and the absence of the attribute represents the false value. @17,1528,694,40
text boolean attributes @17,1580,694,21
text If the attribute is present, its value must either be the empty string or a value that is an match for the attribute's canonical name, with no leading or trailing whitespace. @17,1613,694,40
link "ASCII case-insensitive" https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive @17,1665,694,21
text The values "true" and "false" are not allowed on boolean attributes. To represent a false value, the attribute has to be omitted altogether. success @17,1698,694,40
