h3 2.3.3 Keywords and enumerated attributes @17,3831,694,19
text Some attributes, called , take on a finite set of states. The state for such an attribute is derived by combining the attribute's value, a set of keyword/state mappings, and three possible special states that can also be given in the specification of the attribute. These special states are the , the , and the . @17,3862,694,60
